    The modest +0.018 GPA Progression Delta is driven by a slight improvement from Previous GPA, not from SSC. 
    Regional disparities are substantial: Barisal outperforms Rangpur by 0.20 GPA points (effect size <em>d</em> = 0.34), and the share of students scoring below 3.5 ranges from 20.8% in Dhaka to 32.5% in Rangpur.
  </div>
</section>

<section id="demographics">
  <h2>Student Demographic Overview</h2>
  <p>The dataset comprises <strong>1,000 students</strong> distributed across Bangladesh's eight administrative divisions. 
  The sample is gender-balanced (51.0% female, 49.0% male) and spans ages 15–18, with the majority (53.0%) aged 15–16. 
  School-type representation is also balanced: 52.4% private and 47.6% public.</p>

